PASS File menu Close uses dirty save/discard/cancel lifecycle and only closes selected tab
PASS native File menu Exit cancellation preserves every document, bytes and checkpoint
PASS save all writes exact original files then checkpoints and destroys once
PASS later file-save failure reports partial save, retains remaining dirty document and resumes editing
PASS new-document exit SaveAs cancellation preserves original state; approved name retains document instance
PASS discard batch abort is atomic across dirty documents and preserves clean third-document checkpoint
PASS discard destroy failure atomically restores removed checkpoints before editable state returns
PASS failed destroy compensation CAS preserves a newer valid checkpoint instead of overwriting it
PASS discard success removes only dirty recovery, retains clean third document and original files
PASS recovery-only choice preserves unsaved bytes without writing original files
